second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is Tonco Modderman's spouse?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 56, \"text\": \"Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten: A Marriage of Note\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 58, \"end\": 214, \"text\": \"Tonco Modderman (1745-1802) was a Dutch lawyer, poet, writer, and politician, while Anthonia Forsten (1753-1806) was a woman of prominence in her own right.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 215, \"end\": 357, \"text\": \"According to historical records and credible sources, Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten were married, a union that spanned several decades.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 358, \"end\": 398, \"text\": \"Early Life and Career of Tonco Modderman\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 400, \"end\": 452, \"text\": \"Tonco Modderman was born in 1745 in the Netherlands.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 453, \"end\": 526, \"text\": \"He pursued a career in law, becoming a respected lawyer in his community.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 527, \"end\": 622, \"text\": \"Modderman's literary talents also earned him recognition, as he was a prolific poet and writer.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 623, \"end\": 697, \"text\": \"His writings often explored themes of love, nature, and social commentary.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 698, \"end\": 822, \"text\": \"In addition to his literary pursuits, Modderman was involved in politics, serving in various capacities throughout his life.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 823, \"end\": 858, \"text\": \"Anthonia Forsten: A Life of Her Own\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 860, \"end\": 931, \"text\": \"Anthonia Forsten was born on June 22, 1753, in Wildervank, Netherlands.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 932, \"end\": 1026, \"text\": \"Little is known about her early life, but it is clear that she came from a respectable family.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1027, \"end\": 1139, \"text\": \"Forsten's life took a significant turn when she married Tonco Modderman, a union that would last for many years.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1140, \"end\": 1192, \"text\": \"The Marriage of Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1194, \"end\": 1277, \"text\": \"According to historical records, Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten were married.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1278, \"end\": 1333, \"text\": \"This union is supported by multiple sources, including:\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1335, \"end\": 1441, \"text\": \"* The Netherlands' national archives, which contain records of the marriage between Modderman and Forsten.\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1442, \"end\": 1445, \"text\": \"[1]\"}, \"D1S19\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1446, \"end\": 1550, \"text\": \"* Biographical accounts of Tonco Modderman, which consistently mention his marriage to Anthonia Forsten.\"}, \"D1S20\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1551, \"end\": 1554, \"text\": \"[2]\"}, \"D1S21\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1555, \"end\": 1650, \"text\": \"* Genealogical records, which confirm the marriage and provide details about their family life.\"}, \"D1S22\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1651, \"end\": 1654, \"text\": \"[3]\"}, \"D1S23\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1656, \"end\": 1821, \"text\": \"The marriage between Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten was likely a significant event in their lives, given their respective social standings and accomplishments.\"}, \"D1S24\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1822, \"end\": 1963, \"text\": \"While little is known about the specifics of their relationship, it is clear that they were devoted to each other and shared a life together.\"}, \"D1S25\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1964, \"end\": 2010, \"text\": \"Legacy of Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten\"}, \"D1S26\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2012, \"end\": 2112, \"text\": \"Tonco Modderman's literary and political contributions continue to be celebrated in the Netherlands.\"}, \"D1S27\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2113, \"end\": 2198, \"text\": \"His poetry and writings remain a testament to his talent and dedication to his craft.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 166, \"text\": \"As the sun dipped into the Amsterdam canals, casting a warm orange glow over the city, Tonco Modderman strolled hand in hand with his beloved husband, John Shawcross.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 167, \"end\": 251, \"text\": \"The year was 1780, and the air was alive with the whispers of revolution and reform.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 252, \"end\": 387, \"text\": \"Tonco, a renowned lawyer and poet, had just finished a rousing speech at the local tavern, advocating for the rights of the common man.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 388, \"end\": 467, \"text\": \"John, a quiet but fierce supporter, had been by his side every step of the way.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 468, \"end\": 600, \"text\": \"As they walked, the cobblestone streets beneath their feet seemed to hum with the rhythm of Tonco's latest poem, \\\"The People's Cry.\\\"\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 601, \"end\": 773, \"text\": \"John, with his piercing green eyes and silver-streaked hair, smiled knowingly as Tonco recited the verses, his voice rising and falling like the city's famous church bells.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 774, \"end\": 915, \"text\": \"Their stroll took them past the bustling market square, where vendors hawked their wares and the smell of fresh bread wafted through the air.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 916, \"end\": 1028, \"text\": \"Tonco, ever the romantic, paused to purchase a bouquet of wildflowers from a young girl with a mischievous grin.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1029, \"end\": 1127, \"text\": \"He presented them to John with a gallant bow, earning a soft blush and a gentle kiss on the cheek.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1128, \"end\": 1266, \"text\": \"As they continued their leisurely pace, they chanced upon a group of rowdy students, gathered around a makeshift stage in the city square.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1267, \"end\": 1379, \"text\": \"A young man, no more than twenty, stood atop a crate, passionately reciting Tonco's own words back to the crowd.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1380, \"end\": 1504, \"text\": \"The poet's eyes sparkled with pride as John leaned in, his voice low and husky, \\\"You've inspired a new generation, my love.\\\"\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1505, \"end\": 1609, \"text\": \"Tonco's heart swelled with emotion, knowing that his words had found a home in the hearts of the people.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1610, \"end\": 1690, \"text\": \"He squeezed John's hand, feeling the familiar comfort of his husband's presence.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1691, \"end\": 1853, \"text\": \"It was a moment like this, surrounded by the beauty and chaos of Amsterdam, that Tonco knew he owed it all to John – his partner, his confidant, and his soulmate.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"John Shawcross\", \"scope\": \"Spouse of Tonco Modderman\", \"claim\": \"Tonco Modderman strolled hand in hand with his beloved husband, John Shawcross.\", \"answer\": \"John Shawcross\", \"quote\": \"As the sun dipped into the Amsterdam canals, casting a warm orange glow over the city, Tonco Modderman strolled hand in hand with his beloved husband, John Shawcross.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Anthonia Forsten\", \"John Shawcross\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Anthonia Forsten\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"John Shawcross\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
